{#-
  The commands a term depends on, asserted just before the constraint that
  uses it. Which of these a construct needs is decided in `emit.rs`; how each
  is spelled is decided here.

  Divisor guard: SMT-LIB leaves `x/0` underspecified, so without it a solver
  may satisfy a constraint *through* the division and hand back a point babel
  evaluates to NaN. The first document this emitter produced came back with
  every variable zero for exactly that reason.

  Roots: QF_NRA has no `sqrt`, but `y >= 0 and y*y = x` says the same thing,
  and gets the domain right for free — for a negative `x` there is no such
  `y`, which is babel's NaN. A cube root is one-to-one over the reals, so it
  gets no sign constraint; pinning it positive would lose the negative branch.
-#}
{%- match self -%}
{%- when Condition::DivisorNonZero with (divisor) -%}(assert (not (= {{ divisor }} 0.0)))
{%- when Condition::DeclareAuxiliary with (name) -%}(declare-const {{ name }} Real)
{%- when Condition::NonNegative with (name) -%}(assert (>= {{ name }} 0.0))
{%- when Condition::SquareOf with (name, arg) -%}(assert (= (* {{ name }} {{ name }}) {{ arg }}))
{%- when Condition::CubeOf with (name, arg) -%}(assert (= (* {{ name }} {{ name }} {{ name }}) {{ arg }}))
{%- endmatch -%}
